--
--   Description
----------------------
-- This test checks the alignment error detection of the receive path.
--
-- 
-- Functional Coverage
----------------------
-- * Checks that the GEM can detect an alignment error
-- * Checks that the GEM calculates CRC on the correct data of a missaligned
--   frame
-- * Checks that the GEM re-alignment buffer can detect missalignment regardless
--   of number of complete bytes in the frame.
--
--  
-- Detailed Test Description
----------------------------
-- 1. Setup DMA wait states for the test.
-- 2. Initialise the GEM for 100Mbits/s 32-bit DMA mode.
-- 3. Enable all interrupts, and then enable receive.
-- 4. Receive a 64 byte frame with correct CRC, that has an extra nibble after 
--    the CRC (i.e. 129 nibbles in total).
--    Ensure that the frame is successfully received, with good status.
-- 5. Receive a 65 byte frame with correct CRC, that has an extra nibble after 
--    the CRC (i.e. 131 nibbles in total).
--    Ensure that the frame is successfully received, with good status.
-- 6. Receive a 64 byte frame with bad CRC, that has an extra nibble after 
--    the CRC (i.e. 129 nibbles in total).
--    Ensure that the frame is dropped.
-- 7. Receive a 65 byte frame with bad CRC, that has an extra nibble after 
--    the CRC (i.e. 131 nibbles in total).
--    Ensure that the frame is dropped.
-- 8. Check statistics for the above operations.
--
-- 9. Enable the strip FCS function in the network control register and
--    repeat the tests again.
--10. Receive a 64 byte frame with correct CRC, that has an extra nibble after 
--    the CRC (i.e. 129 nibbles in total).
--    Ensure that the frame is successfully received, with good status.
--11. Receive a 65 byte frame with correct CRC, that has an extra nibble after 
--    the CRC (i.e. 131 nibbles in total).
--    Ensure that the frame is successfully received, with good status.
--12. Receive a 64 byte frame with bad CRC, that has an extra nibble after 
--    the CRC (i.e. 129 nibbles in total).
--    Ensure that the frame is dropped.
--13. Receive a 65 byte frame with bad CRC, that has an extra nibble after 
--    the CRC (i.e. 131 nibbles in total).
--    Ensure that the frame is dropped.
--14. Receive a 64 byte frame with good CRC, and no extra nibbles.
--    Ensure that the frame is successfully received, with good status.
--15. Check statistics for the above operations.
-- 
--16. Keep strip FCS function enabled and repeat the tests again, but this time
--    adjust the amount of preamble so that the realignment buffer overflows.
--17. Receive a 64 byte frame with correct CRC, that has an extra nibble after 
--    the CRC (i.e. 129 nibbles in total).
--    Ensure amount of preamble causes this test to activate the overflow
--    of the alignment buffer in gem_rx. Because the length is a multiple of
--    2 bytes there will not be an additional force alignment on the last data.
--    Ensure that the frame is successfully received, with good status.
--18. Receive a 65 byte frame with correct CRC, that has an extra nibble after 
--    the CRC (i.e. 131 nibbles in total).
--    Ensure amount of preamble causes this test to activate the overflow
--    of the alignment buffer in gem_rx. Because the length is not a multiple of
--    2 bytes there will be an additional force alignment on the last data.
--    Ensure that the frame is successfully received, with good status.
--19. Receive a 64 byte frame with bad CRC, that has an extra nibble after 
--    the CRC (i.e. 129 nibbles in total).
--    Ensure amount of preamble causes this test to activate the overflow
--    of the alignment buffer in gem_rx. Because the length is a multiple of
--    2 bytes there will not be an additional force alignment on the last data.
--    Ensure that the frame is dropped.
--20. Receive a 65 byte frame with bad CRC, that has an extra nibble after 
--    the CRC (i.e. 131 nibbles in total).
--    Ensure amount of preamble causes this test to activate the overflow
--    of the alignment buffer in gem_rx. Because the length is not a multiple of
--    2 bytes there will be an additional force alignment on the last data.
--    Ensure that the frame is dropped.
--21. Receive a 64 byte frame with good CRC, and no extra nibbles.
--    Ensure that the frame is successfully received, with good status.
--22. Check statistics for the above operations.
-- 
--23. Keep strip FCS function enabled and repeat the tests again, but this time
--    as well as adjusting the amount of preamble so that the realignment 
--    buffer overflows, also enable a one byte rx offset.
--24. Receive a 64 byte frame with correct CRC, that has an extra nibble after 
--    the CRC (i.e. 129 nibbles in total).
--    Ensure amount of preamble causes this test to activate the overflow
--    of the alignment buffer in gem_rx. Because the length is a multiple of
--    2 bytes there will not be an additional force alignment on the last data.
--    Ensure that the frame is successfully received, with good status.
--25. Receive a 65 byte frame with correct CRC, that has an extra nibble after 
--    the CRC (i.e. 131 nibbles in total).
--    Ensure amount of preamble causes this test to activate the overflow
--    of the alignment buffer in gem_rx. Because the length is not a multiple of
--    2 bytes there will be an additional force alignment on the last data.
--    Ensure that the frame is successfully received, with good status.
--26. Receive a 64 byte frame with bad CRC, that has an extra nibble after 
--    the CRC (i.e. 129 nibbles in total).
--    Ensure amount of preamble causes this test to activate the overflow
--    of the alignment buffer in gem_rx. Because the length is a multiple of
--    2 bytes there will not be an additional force alignment on the last data.
--    Ensure that the frame is dropped.
--27. Receive a 65 byte frame with bad CRC, that has an extra nibble after 
--    the CRC (i.e. 131 nibbles in total).
--    Ensure amount of preamble causes this test to activate the overflow
--    of the alignment buffer in gem_rx. Because the length is not a multiple of
--    2 bytes there will be an additional force alignment on the last data.
--    Ensure that the frame is dropped.
--28. Receive a 64 byte frame with good CRC, and no extra nibbles.
--    Ensure that the frame is successfully received, with good status.
--29. Check statistics for the above operations.
-- 
--30. Keep strip FCS function enabled and the offset at one byte, and repeat 
--    the tests again, but this time adjusting the amount of preamble so that 
--    the realignment buffer does not overflow overflow.
--31. Receive a 64 byte frame with correct CRC, that has an extra nibble after 
--    the CRC (i.e. 129 nibbles in total).
--    Ensure that the frame is successfully received, with good status.
--32. Receive a 65 byte frame with correct CRC, that has an extra nibble after 
--    the CRC (i.e. 131 nibbles in total).
--    Ensure that the frame is successfully received, with good status.
--33. Receive a 64 byte frame with bad CRC, that has an extra nibble after 
--    the CRC (i.e. 129 nibbles in total).
--    Ensure that the frame is dropped.
--34. Receive a 65 byte frame with bad CRC, that has an extra nibble after 
--    the CRC (i.e. 131 nibbles in total).
--    Ensure that the frame is dropped.
--35. Receive a 64 byte frame with good CRC, and no extra nibbles.
--    Ensure that the frame is successfully received, with good status.
--36. Check statistics for the above operations.
-- 
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- *****************************************************************************
-- 1. Setup DMA wait states for the test.
-- *****************************************************************************
wait_states     3
bus_grant_delay 3


-- *****************************************************************************
-- 2. Initialise the GEM for 100Mbits/s 32-bit DMA mode.
-- 3. Enable all interrupts, and then enable receive.
-- *****************************************************************************
apbrd(100) 00 00000000  -- check reset value of network control register
apbrd      24 00000000  -- check interrupt status
apbwr      28 ffffffff  -- enable all interrupts
apbrd      24 00000000  -- check interrupt status
apbwr      98 12345678  -- specific address register 1 bottom
apbwr      9C 00001111  -- specific address register 1 top
apbrd      04 00080000  -- check reset value of network config register
apbwr      04 00080000  -- 32 bit AHB
apbrd      04 00080000  -- check new value of network config register
apbrd      08 00000006  -- check reset value of network status register
apbrd      18 00000000  -- check reset value of receive queue pointer
apbwr      18 fffff000  -- write receive queue pointer
apbrd      18 fffff000  -- check receive queue pointer
apbwr      00 00000004  -- enable receive
apbrd      20 00000000  -- check contents of the receive status register


-- *****************************************************************************
-- 4. Receive a 64 byte frame with correct CRC, that has an extra nibble after 
--    the CRC (i.e. 129 nibbles in total).
--    Ensure that the frame is successfully received, with good status.
-- *****************************************************************************

apbrdf     20 00000000  "Scenario 1 : 64 byte + 1 nibble, good CRC"
                        -- check contents of the receive status register and 
                        -- trigger reception of frame

rxd(apb)     55d578563412111111112222222233333333
rxd              44444444555555556666666677777777
rxd              8888888899999999aaaaaaaabbbbbbbb
rxd              ccccccccddddddddeeeeeeee
rxd              9e6207c3  -- good CRC
rxd              c         -- extra nibble!

-- Check memory accesses
